Optionally take the position of a DFT pen from the centroid (PositionCentroidX, PositionCentroidY)

The parabola through the three strongest antennas has an error that repeats with the antenna
pitch. Measured on the Surface Pro 9 with the Slim Pen 2 it is small on the X axis (antennas
4.07 mm apart, standard deviation 0.011 .. 0.018 mm against what Windows computes from the same
frames) and larger on the Y axis (0.030 .. 0.052 mm), where the centroid of the same three
antennas does better (0.021 .. 0.025 mm); on X the centroid is worse (0.064 mm).

PositionCentroidX and PositionCentroidY select the centroid per axis for the MPP v2 position
windows (ExtraPositionWindows); CentroidExp is the power of the amplitude. At the screen edge,
where an antenna is missing, the parabola stays. Off by default.

With the centroid on Y only: median distance to Windows' position before its filter 0.035 ..
0.049 mm (0.040 .. 0.064 mm with the parabola on both axes), 90 % within 0.056 .. 0.072 mm
(0.069 .. 0.114 mm).

